* Ten-Tec 80285 broadband magnetics starting models
* Source for topology only: Model 540 manual PDF p. 43 / printed 3-27.
* The winding inductances, turns ratios, DCR, capacitance and coupling are
* not published. All defaults below are estimates for initial simulation.
*
* L85-1/L85-2 use one continuous winding each, with a tap; the split
* inductances scale as the square of the fraction of turns. End-to-end
* 10 uH gives about 220 ohms at 3.5 MHz. The tap starts one third of the
* turns from the supply end, as suggested by its position on the drawing.
* Coupling near unity represents the two sections sharing one core.
* Pins: 1 supply end, 2 collector end, 3 tap.
.subckt DRV80285_TAPPED 1 2 3 params: LEND=10u F=0.333333 KCOUP=0.99 RDC=0.25 CP=3p
Rtop 1 winding_top {RDC*F}
Ltop winding_top 3 {LEND*F*F}
Lbottom 3 winding_bottom {LEND*(1-F)*(1-F)}
Rbottom winding_bottom 2 {RDC*(1-F)}
Ktap Ltop Lbottom {KCOUP}
Cwinding 1 2 {CP}
.ends DRV80285_TAPPED
*
* T85-1 has separate primary and secondary windings. Starting ratio
* Np:Ns=2:1 reflects a 50-ohm fixture load as about 200 ohms at midband.
* The factory drawing does not specify relative winding polarity.
* Pins: 1 supply, 2 collector, 3 secondary return, 4 secondary OUT.
.subckt DRV80285_OUTPUT 1 2 3 4 params: LP=10u LS=2.5u KCOUP=0.97 RP=0.2 RS=0.1 CP=4p CS=4p
Rprimary 1 primary {RP}
Lprimary primary 2 {LP}
Rsecondary 4 secondary {RS}
Lsecondary secondary 3 {LS}
Kwindings Lprimary Lsecondary {KCOUP}
Cprimary 1 2 {CP}
Csecondary 4 3 {CS}
.ends DRV80285_OUTPUT
